 <title>Reassembling meat products</title>
 <link>https://coveredinbees.org.archived.website/node/418</link>
 <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.guardian.co.uk/commentisfree/2013/jan/24/cost-cheap-burger-higher-12p&quot;&gt;Fascinating breakdown&lt;/a&gt; of how cheap burgers are broken down and reassembled by Felicity Lawrence. They are &quot;allowed to contain fat, collagen and connective tissue in the same proportion as they naturally occur in the cut being used&quot; - but the actual source of those additives can and does come from anywhere: &quot;a reconstruction of deconstructed parts, bought around the world from wherever is cheapest. Exchange rate fluctuations might affect where you want to buy your components from week to week.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
