 <title>Boiling stones, feeding cars</title>
 <link>https://coveredinbees.org.archived.website/node/261</link>
 <description>&lt;p&gt;Stuffed and Starved &lt;a href=&quot;http://stuffedandstarved.org/drupal/node/495&quot;&gt;has an article&lt;/a&gt;, written for the &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.thenation.com/doc/20090921/patel_et_al&quot;&gt;The Nation&lt;/a&gt;, that compares Bill Gates&#039; Alliance for a Green Revolution in Africa (AGRA, better funded than many government programs) with the earlier post-second-world-war one. (Which was also a magnate-sponsored affair.) In a &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.coveredinbees.org/node/247&quot;&gt;previous post&lt;/a&gt; I said:&lt;/p&gt;
